[test-suite name=crypto ring=1
  [doc [#
conformance fixtures for cx-stdlib/crypto (spec/std-lib/crypto.md §6).

   Each program imports the bundled module via [?lib 'cx-stdlib/crypto']
   (resolver MUST be quoted) and, where a byte result must be rendered or a
   hex/utf8 input must be constructed, also [?lib 'cx-stdlib/bytes']. The
   LAST expression is the rendered result.

   Keys / messages / MACs / salts / IKM / PRK / info / OKM / signatures /
   ciphertexts are all CXDM bytes (§2.1). Byte inputs are built with
   bytes/from-string-utf8 or bytes/from-hex; byte results are rendered as
   stable lowercase hex via bytes/to-hex, or asserted structurally via
   bytes/length / bytes/equals when an exact golden is not grounded in the
   spec/RFCs.

   Determinism: pure single-shot HMAC / HKDF / keyed-BLAKE3 and ed25519-sign
   are pinned to RFC golden vectors where available. The four impure
   generating surfaces (aead-encrypt, ed25519-keypair, x25519-keypair,
   password-hash) draw fresh randomness (§2.4) and are NEVER asserted by
   literal value: fixtures pin only format / length / round-trip / error.

   Grounded vectors:
     RFC 4231 Test Case 2 (key="Jefe", msg="what do ya want for nothing?"):
       hmac-sha256 = 5bdcc146bf60754e6a042426089575c75a003f089d2739839dec58b964ec3843
       hmac-sha384 = af45d2e376484031617f78d2b58a6b1b9c7ef464f5a01b47e42ec3736322445e8e2240ca5e69e2c78b3239ecfab21649
       hmac-sha512 = 164b7a7bfcf819e2e395fbe73b56e0a387bd64222e831fd610270cd7ea2505549758bf75c05a994a6d034f65f8f0e6fdcaeab1a34d4a6b4b636e070a38bce737
     RFC 5869 Test Case 1 (SHA-256):
       ikm  = 0b*22, salt = 000102030405060708090a0b0c, info = f0f1f2f3f4f5f6f7f8f9, L=42
       PRK  = 077709362c2e32df0ddc3f0dc47bba6390b6c73bb50f9c3122ec844ad7c2b3e5
       OKM  = 3cb25f25faacd57a90434f64d0362f2a2d2d0a90cf1a5a4c5db02d56ecc4c5bf34007208d5b887185865

   Id ranges:
     001-006  HMAC single-shot RFC 4231 vectors + empty-message edge
     007-010  HMAC streaming == single-shot + purity
     011-015  keyed-BLAKE3 + blake3-mac-verify (§3.3, §3.6)
     016-024  HKDF extract/expand/oneshot RFC 5869 + identity + bounds
     025-028  hmac-verify constant-time contract (§3.6)
     029-035  AEAD round-trip / freshness / tamper / errors (§3.7)
     036-044  Ed25519 + X25519 (§3.8)
     045-049  Argon2id password hashing (§3.9)
     050-058  capability-GRANTED behavior twins (grant='random', §2.4): the
              four impure generating surfaces under a least-privilege random
              grant — round-trip / structural-length / verify outcomes
              (deterministic despite fresh entropy). Effort-B granted-harness
              lane; the 029-049 denial twins keep the no-cap CXER0271 contract.
#]]

 [case id=crypto-001-hmac-sha256-rfc4231-tc2 level=core
  [tags crypto hmac-sha256 rfc4231 golden]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/crypto']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/bytes']
[$bytes:to-hex [$crypto:hmac-sha256 [$bytes:from-string-utf8 "Jefe"] [$bytes:from-string-utf8 "what do ya want for nothing?"]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
'5bdcc146bf60754e6a042426089575c75a003f089d2739839dec58b964ec3843'
#]]
 ]

